{"ts": 0.220707, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands, streams, composition\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93mtask\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 227}
{"ts": 0.220742, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.222522, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 4 — GATE TASK\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nWork inside \u001b[94m/var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-ccqi4nor/stage4\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\nDo these:\r\n\r\n  1. Use \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m and a pipe to count from 1 to 100 and save\r\n     the count to \u001b[94mcount.txt\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n  2. Use a glob to list every \u001b[94m*.txt\u001b[0m file in this folder.\r\n\r\nThen type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mI will check: count.txt exists and contains 100, and that you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mlisted the .txt files with a glob.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m when done.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 529}
{"ts": 0.222935, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
{"ts": 0.23842, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[95mcheck\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ test your work\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mshow\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ the task again\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mquit\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ save and leave\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
{"ts": 0.238471, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004h", "len": 8}
